WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.260
My first sewing machine that I owned came through 4-H.

2
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.660
I think it was a project or something they had with Sears.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.960
Sears or Singer, one of them, I can’t remember.

4
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:17.760
4-H purchased . . . either the county office or the parish office purchased the sewing machine,

5
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:24.860
and you could get the sewing machine, you’d have to sign papers and everything like that and then you’d pay them back.

6
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.380
You’d pay the foundation back.

7
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.480
And I remember my mom, we paid seven dollars a week . . . or seven dollars a month,

8
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.760
one of them, until we paid it back.

9
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.260
I still have that sewing machine.

10
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.420
You still have that sewing machine?

11
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.800
Oh, it’s been long.

12
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.460
Did you sew and make earnings from that sewing machine?

13
00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:48.240
Paid for all of my senior stuff by sewing for people.

14
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.610
What kinds of things would you sew for people?

15
00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.410
Oh, everything.

16
00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.550
Made mostly ladies’ clothes.

17
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.090
I didn’t get too much into men’s clothes.

18
00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.970
Didn’t get too much into that.

19
00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:09.150
I actually had a best friend and her mother that I sewed a lot for and everything, then I’d sewed for other people,

20
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:16.910
but I sewed for them all the way through high school until probably my freshman year in college.

21
00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:21.770
And then at that point in time, I kind of, I do special things for people.

22
00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.590
You know, evening dresses or a suit or anything like that.

23
00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:28.890
All the way through high school I sewed on a regular basis.

24
00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.350
I didn’t like the hand stitching.

25
00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.870
My mother used to do that.

26
00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:35.170
My mother would do the hand work.

27
00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.250
I guess you’d call us a team.
